 "summary": "The asymptotic statements match Abramowitz\u2013Stegun 10.1.16: base cases (x\u00b7j\u2080 = sin x, x\u00b7j\u2081 \u2212 sin(x\u2212\u03c0/2) = sin x/x) and the induction through mul_sphericalBesselJ_add_two with sin(x\u2212(l+2)\u03c0/2) = \u2212sin(x\u2212l\u03c0/2) all check out, as does the derivative form via deriv_sphericalBesselJ_of_ne_zero and sin(x\u2212(l+1)\u03c0/2) = \u2212cos(x\u2212l\u03c0/2). The cocompact \u211d filter is justified rather than cosmetic, since (\u22121)^l parity makes the same shifted sine correct at both ends, and the helper lemmas in Cocompact.lean are true, non-vacuous, and rest on existing upstream facts.",
